(Library opening hours. The Hartley Library on the Northfield campus is open from 08:00) Tj T*
(to 23:00 Monday to Friday during term time, and from 10:00 to 18:00 at weekends. During) Tj T*
(the summer vacation the library closes at 20:00 on weekdays and is closed on Sundays.) Tj T*
(The 24-hour study centre on level two stays open all night, every day of the year, and) Tj T*
(is accessible with a valid student card. Group study rooms can be booked online up to) Tj T*
(seven days in advance, for a maximum of three hours per booking.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Book borrowing and renewals. Undergraduates may borrow up to 12 items at a time,) Tj T*
(postgraduates up to 25, and staff up to 40. Standard loans last 21 days and renew) Tj T*
(automatically up to three times unless another reader has reserved the item. Reserved) Tj T*
(items must be returned within seven days. The daily overdue charge is 0.40 GBP per item,) Tj T*
(capped at 15 GBP per item. Items borrowed through the inter-library loan service are) Tj T*
(held for collection for ten days and cannot be renewed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(IT helpdesk and account support. The IT helpdesk in the Sinclair Building answers calls) Tj T*
(from 07:30 to 20:00 Monday to Friday and from 09:00 to 16:00 on Saturdays. It is closed) Tj T*
(on Sundays and on public holidays. Password resets can be completed online through the) Tj T*
(self-service portal at any time. Hardware faults are logged as tickets and the target) Tj T*
(response is one working day for staff and two working days for students. Lost student) Tj T*
(cards are replaced at the helpdesk for a fee of 12 GBP, and the replacement is printed) Tj T*
(while you wait.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Wi-Fi and network access. The campus wireless network is called Northfield-Secure and) Tj T*
(requires your student account credentials. Eduroam is available in all teaching) Tj T*
(buildings. Wired connections in halls of residence are provided by the accommodation) Tj T*
(provider, not by the university, and faults should be reported to the hall reception.) Tj T*
(Streaming services are rate-limited between 18:00 and midnight on the shared network.) Tj T*
(Virtual private network access is required for library databases from off campus, and) Tj T*
(the client is available for Windows, macOS and Linux.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Tuition fees and payment deadlines. Undergraduate tuition for home students is 9,250 GBP) Tj T*
(per year. International undergraduate tuition is 21,400 GBP per year, and postgraduate) Tj T*
(taught tuition is 24,900 GBP per year. Fees may be paid in full at enrolment or in three) Tj T*
(instalments due on 15 October, 15 January and 15 April. A late payment charge of 1.5) Tj T*
(percent per month applies to unpaid instalments after 14 days. Students experiencing) Tj T*
(financial difficulty should contact the money advice team before the deadline rather) Tj T*
(than after it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Scholarships and bursaries. The Northfield Merit Scholarship pays 3,000 GBP per year to) Tj T*
(entrants with three A grades at A level or equivalent, and is renewed automatically if) Tj T*
(the student averages 65 percent or higher. The Hardship Bursary is means-tested and) Tj T*
(awards between 500 and 2,500 GBP per year; applications open on 1 September and close on) Tj T*
(31 October. Care-leaver support covers accommodation costs in full for the first year.) Tj T*
(Scholarships are not repayable and do not affect eligibility for a student loan.) Tj T*
