(Accommodation fees and contracts. University-managed halls cost between 128 and 176 GBP) Tj T*
(per week including utilities and internet. Contracts run for 44 weeks for undergraduates) Tj T*
(and 51 weeks for postgraduates. A deposit of 400 GBP is required to secure a room and is) Tj T*
(refunded within 28 days of the end of the contract, less any damage charges.) Tj T*
(Cancellation is free within 14 days of accepting the offer. Private rental accommodation) Tj T*
(is not covered by the university contract and disputes are handled by the students') Tj T*
(union advice service.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Examination rules. Students must arrive 15 minutes before an examination starts.) Tj T*
(Admission after 30 minutes past the start time is refused. Only transparent water) Tj T*
(bottles and approved calculators may be taken to the desk; bags are left at the back of) Tj T*
(the hall. Mobile phones must be switched off and stored, not merely silenced. A) Tj T*
(candidate who is ill should submit a mitigating circumstances form within five working) Tj T*
(days with medical evidence, rather than sit the examination and appeal the mark) Tj T*
(afterwards.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Assessment, marking and grade bands. Undergraduate modules are marked on a percentage) Tj T*
(scale: 70 and above is a first, 60 to 69 an upper second, 50 to 59 a lower second, 40 to) Tj T*
(49 a third, and below 40 a fail. Postgraduate modules require 50 percent to pass and 70) Tj T*
(for a distinction. Marks are provisional until the examination board meets in June.) Tj T*
(Coursework is returned within 15 working days of the deadline. A module mark is capped) Tj T*
(at 40 when it is passed on a resit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Extensions, late submission and mitigating circumstances. Coursework submitted after the) Tj T*
(published deadline loses 10 percent of the available marks per working day, up to a) Tj T*
(maximum of five days, after which it scores zero. Self-certified extensions of up to) Tj T*
(seven days are available once per academic year for eligible modules. Longer extensions) Tj T*
(require evidence and the module leader's approval. Mitigating circumstances are) Tj T*
(submitted to the faculty office, not to the module leader, within five working days of) Tj T*
(the assessment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Academic integrity and misconduct. All submitted work must be the student's own.) Tj T*
(Contract cheating, including paying another person to write an assignment, is a category) Tj T*
(one offence and normally results in exclusion from the programme. Unacknowledged use of) Tj T*
(another author's words or ideas is plagiarism, whether the source is a book, a web page) Tj T*
(or a generative artificial intelligence tool. Using an AI tool to produce assessed work) Tj T*
(without permission is treated as misconduct. The university's similarity checking) Tj T*
(service compares submissions against a database of previous work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Attendance and leave of absence. Attendance at timetabled sessions is recorded and) Tj T*
(students on a student visa must attend at least 80 percent of scheduled contact hours to) Tj T*
(comply with sponsorship conditions. Absence through illness of more than seven days) Tj T*
(needs a medical certificate. A leave of absence may be granted for one academic year in) Tj T*
(exceptional circumstances, and the request must be made before the end of the second) Tj T*
(teaching week. Returning students re-enter at the same stage of the programme.) Tj T*
