(Student support and counselling. The wellbeing service offers free, confidential) Tj T*
(counselling and is open from 09:00 to 17:00 Monday to Friday in the Lawson Centre.) Tj T*
(Appointments can be booked online or by telephone, and urgent same-day appointments are) Tj T*
(available each morning. The service does not provide crisis care outside office hours;) Tj T*
(the emergency number for the campus security team operates continuously. Disability) Tj T*
(support arranges adjustments such as extra time in examinations, and applications should) Tj T*
(be made at least six weeks before the assessment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Health services and emergencies. The campus health centre is a general practice surgery) Tj T*
(and requires registration; it is open 08:30 to 18:00 on weekdays. For emergencies call) Tj T*
(999. The campus security team can be reached on the internal extension 2222 at any hour) Tj T*
(and can summon an ambulance. A defibrillator is located in the entrance of every) Tj T*
(teaching building. International students who pay the immigration health surcharge are) Tj T*
(entitled to use National Health Service treatment on the same basis as residents.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(International student office and visas. The international office in the Ashworth) Tj T*
(Building advises on visas, immigration and working restrictions. Students on a student) Tj T*
(visa may work up to 20 hours per week during term time and full time in the vacations.) Tj T*
(Registration with the police is required for nationals of certain countries and must be) Tj T*
(completed within seven days of arrival. The office issues attendance letters for visa) Tj T*
(applications within three working days. Visa advice is free; the office cannot give) Tj T*
(legal advice on immigration appeals.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Clubs, societies and sports. The students' union recognises more than 140 societies.) Tj T*
(Membership fees are set by each society and typically range from 3 to 25 GBP per year.) Tj T*
(The sports centre offers a student membership of 180 GBP per year or 6 GBP per visit,) Tj T*
(and includes the swimming pool, gym and courts. Club transport to away fixtures is) Tj T*
(subsidised by 50 percent. New societies need 15 registered members and a constitution) Tj T*
(approved by the union, and can apply for a start-up grant of up to 150 GBP.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Careers service and placements. The careers service runs drop-in sessions from 10:00 to) Tj T*
(16:00 on weekdays and offers one-to-one appointments with a careers adviser. Placement) Tj T*
(years are arranged through the faculty placement office and must be approved before the) Tj T*
(end of the second year. Students on a placement year pay a reduced tuition fee of 1,850) Tj T*
(GBP. The service reviews applications and runs mock interviews, but does not guarantee) Tj T*
(an interview or a placement.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Complaints and academic appeals. A complaint about a service should first be raised) Tj T*
(informally with the relevant department. A formal complaint must be submitted within 20) Tj T*
(working days using the online form. Academic appeals are limited to procedural) Tj T*
(irregularity, new evidence not available at the time, or bias; disagreeing with the) Tj T*
(academic judgement of an examiner is not grounds for appeal. Appeals must be lodged) Tj T*
