(Graduation and awards. Graduation ceremonies are held in July and December in the) Tj T*
(Northfield Assembly Hall. Students must have completed all assessments and cleared any) Tj T*
(outstanding debt to the university before a certificate is issued. Guest tickets are) Tj T*
(limited to two per graduand and additional tickets are allocated by ballot. Academic) Tj T*
(dress hire costs 45 GBP and must be ordered at least 14 days before the ceremony. Degree) Tj T*
(certificates are posted within eight weeks of the ceremony.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Parking and campus transport. Student parking permits cost 120 GBP per year and are) Tj T*
(allocated by lottery because demand exceeds supply; students living within two miles of) Tj T*
(campus are not eligible. Visitors pay 1.60 GBP per hour in the pay-and-display car park.) Tj T*
(The campus shuttle runs every 15 minutes from 07:00 to 22:00 between the main site and) Tj T*
(the halls. Bicycle storage is free and covered, and a repair stand is available outside) Tj T*
(the sports centre. Parking fines are 40 GBP, reduced to 20 GBP if paid within 14 days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Printing, copying and study spaces. Students receive a printing credit of 5 GBP per) Tj T*
(term, which covers approximately 250 black-and-white pages. Additional credit is) Tj T*
(purchased online at 0.02 GBP per page for black and white and 0.08 GBP for colour.) Tj T*
(Printers are located on every floor of the library and in the Sinclair Building. Silent) Tj T*
(study floors are levels three and four; group discussion is permitted on level two.) Tj T*
(Poster printing is handled by the media centre and requires three working days' notice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Laboratory and workshop safety. Safety glasses and laboratory coats are mandatory in all) Tj T*
(wet laboratories. Food and drink are prohibited. Students must complete the online) Tj T*
(induction before their first practical session and must not work alone outside staffed) Tj T*
(hours. Accidents, however minor, must be reported to the technician on duty and recorded) Tj T*
(in the accident book. Waste chemicals are disposed of in the labelled containers only;) Tj T*
(sinks are not for chemical disposal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Data protection and student records. The university processes personal data under the UK) Tj T*
(General Data Protection Regulation. Students may request a copy of their records through) Tj T*
(a subject access request, which is answered within one month. Contact details are shared) Tj T*
(with the students' union unless the student opts out. Examination scripts are retained) Tj T*
(for 12 months and then destroyed. Name changes must be supported by documentary evidence) Tj T*
(and are processed within ten working days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Religious observance and diversity. The multi-faith chaplaincy in the Old Chapel) Tj T*
(provides prayer rooms, quiet space and confidential conversation for students of any) Tj T*
(religion or none. Prayer facilities are open from 07:00 to 22:00 and include washing) Tj T*
(areas. Students may request timetable adjustments for religious festivals by contacting) Tj T*
(the faculty office at least 14 days in advance. The equality and diversity team advises) Tj T*
(on harassment and discrimination complaints, which can also be reported anonymously) Tj T*
